=== SCHEMA ===
migrations/000168_vehicle_unit_history.up.sql defines:
  CREATE TABLE vehicle_unit_history (
    id              BIGSERIAL,
    vehicle_id      BIGINT      NOT NULL,
    unit_kind       TEXT        NOT NULL,
    unit_value      TEXT        NOT NULL,
    effective_from  TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    source          TEXT        NOT NULL,
    CHECK (unit_kind IN ('distance','temperature','pressure','charge')),
    CHECK (source    IN ('telemetry','rest_bootstrap','manual')),
    PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_id, unit_kind, effective_from, id),
    UNIQUE (vehicle_id, unit_kind, effective_from, unit_value, source)
  );
  CREATE INDEX vehicle_unit_history_lookup
    ON vehicle_unit_history (vehicle_id, unit_kind, effective_from DESC, id DESC);

WHY id is part of PK + tiebreaker:
  bootstrap (time.Now()) and telemetry (atomic.EmittedAt) can collide
  at the same effective_from second. Without ORDER BY id DESC, two
  pods could resolve different "active" units for the same t. ORDER
  BY effective_from DESC, id DESC guarantees the latest-inserted row
  at the same instant wins everywhere.

WHY UNIQUE includes (effective_from, value, source):
  Idempotency rule: two distinct sources at the same instant ARE
  legitimate distinct rows (e.g. bootstrap and telemetry agreeing at
  process start). Re-running bootstrap or replaying a payload is a
  no-op INSERT via ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, but a NEW source at the
  same instant still writes its own row.

migrations/000168_vehicle_unit_history.down.sql:
  DROP TABLE IF EXISTS vehicle_unit_history;
  (Restoring requires re-running REST bootstrap (prompt 0023) +
   organic Setting*Unit replay from MQTT.)

=== DESIGN ===

PACKAGE LAYOUT
  types.go   constants (Kind, Source, AllKinds/AllSources), Entry,
             ErrNotFound, prometheus invalidateFailuresTotal counter
             with public name tesla_unit_history_invalidate_failures_total.
  repo.go    Repo interface (Record/At/Latest), pgRepo (pgxpool-backed),
             dbtx interface mirroring internal/database.DBTX, SQL
             constants (recordSQL, atSQL, latestSQL).
  cache.go   Cache type, redisClient interface, payload JSON shape,
             keyFor() helper (literal "unit_history:" prefix), Get/Put/
             Invalidate methods implementing the layered L0/L1/L2 model
             from ADR-004 #4.

CONSTRUCTOR
  NewRepo(db dbtx, cache *Cache) Repo
    cache may be nil (degraded / test mode); reads fall through to PG
    and writes skip the invalidate step.

REPO METHODS
  Record(ctx, e Entry) error
    1. Validate (vehicle_id != 0, kind/value/source not empty,
       effective_from not zero) — fast-fail before touching PG.
    2. Normalize effective_from to UTC.
    3. INSERT INTO vehicle_unit_history (vehicle_id, unit_kind,
       unit_value, effective_from, source) VALUES ($1,$2,$3,$4,$5)
       ON CONFLICT (vehicle_id, unit_kind, effective_from, unit_value,
       source) DO NOTHING.
    4. After successful PG commit: cache.Invalidate(vehicleID, kind).
       Redis DEL failure logged + counted via
       tesla_unit_history_invalidate_failures_total{reason="redis_del"}
       but NOT propagated.

  At(ctx, vehicleID, kind, t) (units.ActiveUnit, error)
    1. Validate inputs.
    2. Cache fast path via Cache.GetForAt — applies validity rule
       (cached entry valid for t only when t >= cached.EffectiveFrom).
    3. On cache miss: SELECT unit_value FROM vehicle_unit_history
       WHERE vehicle_id=$1 AND unit_kind=$2 AND effective_from <= $3
       ORDER BY effective_from DESC, id DESC LIMIT 1.
    4. pgx.ErrNoRows -> ErrNotFound. Caller drops + bumps a counter.

  Latest(ctx, vehicleID, kind) (Entry, error)
    1. Cache fast path via Cache.GetLatest (no validity rule).
    2. On cache miss: SELECT unit_value, effective_from, source FROM
       vehicle_unit_history WHERE vehicle_id=$1 AND unit_kind=$2
       ORDER BY effective_from DESC, id DESC LIMIT 1.
    3. On PG hit: cache.PutLatest populates L0+L1.
    4. pgx.ErrNoRows -> ErrNotFound.

CACHE LAYERS (cache.go)
  L0  per-process sync.Map keyed by (vehicleID, kind), entries carry
      cachedAt for TTL eviction (CacheTTL = 60s).
  L1  Redis key unit_history:{vehicleID}:{kind}, EX 60, value is
      JSON {value, effective_from, source}.
  L2  PostgreSQL vehicle_unit_history (canonical).

CACHE-INVALIDATION CONTRACT (ADR-004 #4 verbatim)
  - On Repo.Record (after PG commit):
      Order: PG commit -> Redis DEL -> local L0 clear.
      DEL failure: log + tesla_unit_history_invalidate_failures_total{reason="redis_del"}++,
      but do NOT propagate or roll back PG insert.
  - On read miss:
      L0 first; if stale, fall through.
      L1 next; on hit, promote to L0; on redis.Nil/err, fall through.
      L2 (PG) reads return canonical; Repo.Latest then PutLatest.
  - Validity rule for At(t):
      cached entry valid for t ONLY when t >= cached.EffectiveFrom.
  - Acceptable consistency window: CacheTTL (60s).

=== UNIT_TEST ===
internal/tesla/unit_history/repo_test.go runs the Repo contract
suite against TWO implementations:
  - memRepo (in-memory) — always runs (no DB needed)
  - pgRepo (live PG)    — runs when DATABASE_URL is set

Suite tests (one t.Run per scenario):
  InsertInAnyOrder_ReadOrderedByEffectiveFrom
  ErrNotFound_WhenNoRowExists
  ErrNotFound_WhenAllRowsAfterT
  SameInstantTiebreaker_LaterInsertedRowWinsViaIdDesc
    (asserts BOTH orderings: PSI-then-Bar -> Bar wins;
     Bar-then-PSI -> PSI wins)
  Idempotency_DuplicateRecordWritesOneRow
    (three identical Records -> rowCount==1)
  Latest_ReturnsHighestEffectiveFromRow
  KindIsolated_DistanceAndTemperatureDoNotInterfere
  VehicleIsolated_TwoVehiclesDoNotShareHistory

Plus pgRepo-specific unit tests with a recording fakeDBTX:
  TestPgRepo_RecordSQL_ContainsOnConflictAndOrdering
  TestPgRepo_Record_RejectsZeroFields (5 subcases)
  TestPgRepo_Record_NormalizesEffectiveFromToUTC
  TestPgRepo_At_PropagatesNotFound
  TestPgRepo_Latest_PropagatesNotFound
  TestKindAndSourceClosedSets (migration-CHECK-mirror invariant)

cache_test.go uses a recording fakeRedisClient (same pattern as
internal/signal/redis_cache_test.go's fakeRedisSignalClient;
miniredis is NOT in the project's go.mod, so an in-tree fake is the
matching pattern):
  TestCache_GetLatest_Miss_ReturnsFalse
  TestCache_PutLatest_ThenGetLatest_Hit
    (validates Set key=unit_history:1:distance, TTL=CacheTTL,
     payload round-trips)
  TestCache_GetForAt_BypassesCacheWhen_t_BeforeEffectiveFrom
    (the validity-rule test the prompt mandates)
  TestCache_GetForAt_BypassPathDoesNotInvalidateCache
  TestCache_Invalidate_DeletesRedisAndLocal
  TestCache_Invalidate_RedisDelFailureIncrementsMetric
  TestCache_GetLatest_TTLExpiry
  TestCache_NilCacheIsNoop
  TestCache_GetLatest_RedisHitPromotesToL0
  TestCache_KeyShape_Stable
  TestCache_GetLatest_RedisErrorFallsThrough

